# Verify kibbles — required gate

Do not claim done on user-facing UI, auth, routing, Inertia pages, or feature work until you have run the project verify skill. This is a hard gate, not optional flavor.

## What to run

1. Read `.agents/skills/verify-kibbles/SKILL.md` first. That is the live path. `.cursor/skills` and `.claude/skills` are symlinks to `.agents/skills` — do not invent a second copy.
2. Follow that skill: doctor when a local server is in play, then the mapped Pest Feature and/or Browser tests, or a prove helper:

```bash
.agents/skills/verify-kibbles/bin/doctor
.agents/skills/verify-kibbles/bin/prove-welcome
.agents/skills/verify-kibbles/bin/prove-dashboard
php artisan test --compact tests/Feature/Controllers/DashboardTest.php tests/Browser/DashboardTest.php
```

3. If Pest Browser complains about missing or outdated Playwright browsers: `bun install` then `bunx playwright install` (or `bunx playwright install chromium`).

## What does not count

- Reading the skill and skipping the commands
- "CI will catch it" without a local run
- A screenshot of a page you did not drive
- Inventing a parallel Playwright CLI or tautological file-content tests

CI (`.github/workflows/tests.yml`) runs `composer test` on every PR to `master` and fails on red. That is the merge gate. It does not replace a local verify-kibbles run before you say the work is done.

Copy, comments-only, and docs-only changes do not need the full Browser suite. Still run the smallest relevant Pest Feature/Unit tests when you change behavior.
